# Thumbnail and title rules (25 Sep 2026)

Readable copy with the evidence: `00_Brand/Channel-Setup/THUMBNAIL_AND_TITLE_RULES.md`. Audit: `00_Brand/Channel-Setup/audits/THUMBNAIL_TITLE_AUDIT_2026-09-25/AUDIT.md`. House thumb gate (from the retired UAT bible, now in `STUDIO_PLAYBOOK.md` §8): yellow hook word + white, centre-safe, no clipped lines, distinct plate, no Orbit.

## Titles

- Use one of six shapes:
  - an ending / countdown (*What Remains After the Last Star Dies?* 622)
  - a body impossibility (*Why You Can't Stand on a Neutron Star* 419)
  - a yes/no about a familiar thing (*Is the Moon Leaving Us?* 290)
  - something hidden (*Why Europa Is Hiding a Massive Ocean* 291)
  - one real number (*Why Does the Moon Drift 3.8 cm a Year?* 253)
  - a specific contradiction (*Why JWST Pictures Don't Match the Textbook*)
- A familiar noun (Moon, Sun, star, sky, Earth, you) in the first four words.
- **FAIL:** hedged claims ("We may have…", "We could…", "might", "What if…"; a yes/no question starting "Could a…?" is fine), descriptions of what something can do, poetic images, hashtags, series suffixes, a copy of an existing public title, threat framing.
- Longs: the searched phrase as a question ("What Happens When…", "What Would You See If…"), keyword in the first five words.
- **News framing is OK on a real new result** (Packaging, 11 Oct 2026): "We Found…", "We Just Saw…", a mission name. Needs a dated result in SOURCES.md; never on an old fact; still no hedge or threat.

## Long thumbs

- One subject filling at least a third of the frame, on a dark, simple background.
- **2–4 words**, readable at 168×94. Run `python3 00_Brand/Channel-Setup/tools/thumb_preview.py long <thumb> --out <sheet>` and look at the small tile.
- The thumb adds to the title. It never repeats it.
- One heavy capitals font on every thumb. Keep text off the subject and out of the bottom-right corner (duration badge).
- Same promise as the title. No Orbit (until a Test & Compare on a long with more than 1,000 impressions says otherwise).
- Set up Test & Compare with 3 variants. Judge CTR only past about 500 impressions.

## Packaging (Astrum study, 11 Oct 2026; THUMBNAIL_AND_TITLE_RULES.md §2.B wins where it differs)

- **Hook text names the object or dares** (THIS IS TRITON, DON'T GO HERE). No vague questions or teasers (WHAT ARE THEY?, HOW LONG?, WHEN THEY MEET). A question only if it names the subject (SIGNAL ON MARS?).
- **2–3 words in a band across the top** (or a clear edge), **never over the subject.** Keep the yellow hook word, white rest, house font and outline.
- **Grade harder:** `thumb_preview.py long <thumb> --out <sheet> --score` must PASS: saturation 100+ (target 120; 85+ with `--pale` for the Moon, Europa ice, Saturn), near-black 30% or less.
- Optional: one small white arrow for a "look at this" discovery, never over the subject's centre.
- Chief / Orbit Auditor score HOOK, BAND, GRADE, PHONE on every new or rebuilt long thumb; any FAIL goes back before it's set.

## Shorts

- **Frame 0 is the thumbnail in the feed** (78% of Shorts views). Median views: world or object at frame 0 86.5, Orbit at frame 0 23.5, dark or text card 16.5.
- Frame-0 caption: the promise in 2–4 words, cap height about 8–10% of frame height (twice today's), yellow hook word.
- Custom Short thumb (search and channel pages): the title's hook words, not a new poetic line. 2–4 words, the stack at least 60% of frame width, vertically centred. Check with `thumb_preview.py short`.
